    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10b-catfishes-suckermouths-plecos-and-l-numbers/hypancistrus_zebra_l_46_double_tailfin_en/",
      "html": "<p>November 2006: At present we can offer, beside normal German-bred zebras (surely the most in-demand of all L-numbers), an individual with a doubled lower caudal fin. This change of the fin is probably due to a disturbance in the embryonic development. If someone hopes to breed a strain of \"veil-tailed zebras\" with this fish, it will probably end in disappointment. Nevertheless: absolutely unusual, a rarity among the L-numbers.</p><p>(Photo F. Schäfer, Text K. Diehl)</p>"
    }
